<title>SPAIN: Spain's CNMV suspends trade in Zabalburu.</title>
<headline>Spain's CNMV suspends trade in Zabalburu.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish stock exchange commission CNMV said on Monday it had suspended trade in the real estate group Inmobiliaria Zabalburu because of special factors that could affect normal business.</p>
<p>On April 30, Hebra, a subsidiary of tobacco group Tabacalera, bought 452,726 shares, or 18.25 percent, of Zabalburu at 2,440 pesetas per share. Hebra now has a 21.18 percent stake in the property firm.</p>
<p>When CNMV suspended trade, Zabalburu shares were trading 370 pesetas higher at 2,970 pesetas.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
